    "innovation": "This paper develops a global, monthly burned area dataset (GFED3) for July 1996 through mid-2009 by merging four satellite products to produce a consistent long-term record of fire activity and its interannual variability.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "GFED2",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SUBSEQUENT_VERSION",
            "target_entity_instance": "GFED3",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "Here we describe the next generation of the Global Fire Emissions Database burned area data set \u2013 GFED3 \u2013 which provides global, monthly burned area aggregated to 0.5\u00b0 spatial resolution from mid-1996 through the present, and is specifically intended for use within large-scale (typically global) atmospheric and biogeochemical models. Unlike existing products, the data set was compiled using inter-calibrated observations from multiple sensors, followed by a correction phase to improve consistency, thus reducing the need for end users to manually stitch together multiple (and potentially inconsistent) burned area data sets over extended time periods. Included in the data set are spatially-explicit uncertainties that reflect the varying quality of the burned area estimates produced from each source and methodol-ogy. Following a summary of the input data in Sect. 2 and a description of our methods in Sect. 3, we use the GFED3 data set to assess the interannual variability and long-term trends in global burned area over the past 13 years in Sect. 4, and then compare it to the independent L3JRC, GLOBCAR-BON, and Collection 5 MODIS MCD45A1 global burned area products in Sect. 5.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "GFED2",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "regional regression trees",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "As an interim product based on a small quantity of 500-m burned area training data, the GFED2 burned area data set was composed solely of indirect burned area estimates derived from gridded active fire counts. In that approach, a series of regional regression trees were used to relate monthly active-fire and ancillary land cover information to monthly area burned at 1\u00ba spatial resolution (Giglio et al., 2006b).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": false
        },
        {
